transcript.message:
It is so hard to admit, but sometimes I feel like I'm hitting a wall that I can't even see. My old toolkit—my meditation practice, my breathing exercises—they used to work like magic. Now? They feel like they're doing nothing but making me more aware of how shaky I am.

I tried meditating this morning, and instead of calming down, I just sat there watching my hands tremble harder, realizing how much power the panic has over my body right now. It feels like no matter what I do, I'm stuck in this loop of "why won't it stop?"

And honestly, part of me feels helpless because I don't know if this is temporary or if I've actually lost all my progress. I keep thinking, *What if this never goes away?* What if I have to start over from day one, maybe even with less success than before? The fear isn't just about the shaking anymore;

